---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, CORRECTION_POLICY_TEXT, OPERATOR_SETUP } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About PluginDrop | Plugin Deals for Music Producers`} description="PluginDrop is operated by SignalDrop — a music producer who tracks manufacturer sales and vendor prices to surface VST plugin deals." />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			"@context": "https://schema.org",
			"@type": "Organization",
			"name": "SignalDrop",
			"url": "https://plugindrop.net",
			"logo": "https://plugindrop.net/images/logo-512.png",
			"description": "SignalDrop operates PluginDrop, a curated VST plugin deal aggregator for music producers.",
			"email": CONTACT_EMAIL,
			"sameAs": ["https://plugindrop.net"]
		})} />
		<style>
			.about {
				max-width: 640px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 3rem 1rem;
			}
			.about h1 {
				font-size: 2rem;
				margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
			}
			.about p {
				color: var(--text-secondary);
				margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
				line-height: 1.7;
			}
			.about strong {
				color: var(--text-primary);
			}
			.about h2 {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				margin-top: 2rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
			}
			.about ul {
				padding-left: 1.5rem;
				color: var(--text-secondary);
			}
			.about li {
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<a href="#main-content" class="sr-only">Skip to content</a>
		<Header />
		<main id="main-content">
			<div class="about">
				<h1>About PluginDrop</h1>
				<p>
					I'm a music producer who got tired of missing plugin deals. So I started
					building a price tracker. PluginDrop's primary sources are <strong>official vendor
					and manufacturer pages</strong> (such as Plugin Boutique and developer stores),
					manufacturer sale announcements, and <strong>my own price tracking</strong> that
					records prices over time. Community posts, such as Reddit threads, are a secondary
					source, mainly used to fill in historical prices — so you don't have to.
				</p>
				<p>
					I curate the best deals based on brand reputation, discount depth,
					product quality, and relevance to producers.
					Only deals worth your time make it to the site.
				</p>

				<h2>What I Cover</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Free VST plugins and sample libraries</li>
					<li>Limited-time sales and flash deals</li>
					<li>In-depth comparisons and roundups</li>
					<li>New releases worth watching</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>My Setup</h2>
				<p>PluginDrop's data pipeline runs alongside a real studio setup:</p>
				<ul>
					{OPERATOR_SETUP.map(({ label, value }) => <li><strong>{label}:</strong> {value}</li>)}
				</ul>

				<h2>Methodology</h2>
				<p>
					PluginDrop doesn't publish hands-on reviews claiming every plugin has been tested.
					Deal quality is judged from tracked price history, discount depth against prices
					I've actually observed over time, and public specs and vendor documentation.
					Deal articles include the date pricing was confirmed —
					I update or remove listings when deals expire.
					See <a href="/how-we-track-prices/">how we track prices</a> for the full methodology.
				</p>

				<h2>Editorial Policy</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Affiliate links are marked with [Ad] where required by law</li>
					<li>Pricing data is confirmed on the date shown in each article</li>
					<li>{CORRECTION_POLICY_TEXT}</li>
					<li>Commission rates have no influence on my deal scoring or recommendations</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Contact</h2>
				<p>PluginDrop is operated by <strong>SignalDrop</strong>. For inquiries, visit the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>

				<h2 id="personalization">Local Personalization</h2>
				<p>
					Some sections (deals, article lists) may be re-ordered based on what you've been
					reading — this happens entirely in your browser (localStorage). Your reading
					profile never leaves your device. Click "reset" next to any "Sorted for you"
					label to clear it.
				</p>

				<h2 id="affiliate">Affiliate Disclosure</h2>
				<p>Some links earn PluginDrop a commission at no extra cost to you. Read the full <a href="/editorial-policy/#affiliate">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
